      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A rare clinical case is described pertaining to a 70-year-old female patient with atherosclerotic cardiosclerosis accompanied by a combination of sinus and ventricular extrasystole. The importance of rhythmography and the criterion of allorhythmia is emphasized as being he indices that help to improve the diagnosis of sinus extrasystole."},
